From: Yusuf İhsan KILINÇ
Subject: [PATCH 0098] anv: xemac fd handle types from what the kernel offers, at runtime

On top of mesa-prod9 (prod8 + 0089-0092 + 0095 + 0096). Built in a copy (src/mesa-fd1, build-fd1.sh, same meson
options as build-prod9, -Dxemac=src/xemac-fd1/user); NOT installed. Stage 0 of fd sharing
(docs/reports/b580-fd-sharing-20261103.md, report b580-fd-sharing-stage0-20261104.md). Needs the xemac of
patches/xemac/fd1-object-fds-syncobj-sync-file-prime-and-fake-device.patch (xemac_fd_sharing, xemac_obj_size).

With xemac (macOS, B580.kext) the fd extensions were off at compile time (ANV_FD_SHARING false): no syncobj fds,
sync files or dma-bufs existed. B580.kext now gets object fds (opens of the clone device /dev/b580obj, one kernel
object per fd; uapi/b580_drm.h B580_CAP_FD_OBJECTS), so the device is asked at physical device creation
(xemac_fd_sharing(): B580_CAP_FD_OBJECTS = 1, and DRM_CAP_PRIME = IMPORT|EXPORT for BO fds):
 - VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd and VK_KHR_external_fence_fd with syncobj fds and sync files (OPAQUE_FD and
   SYNC_FD come together: vk_semaphore/vk_fence derive both from the drm_syncobj sync type, and a shared binary
   semaphore's move goes through a sync file),
 - VK_KHR_external_memory_fd with PRIME fds.
An older kernel (or XEMAC_FDS=0) reports neither and the device is exactly as before. VK_EXT_external_memory_dma_buf
(stage 3) and VK_EXT_physical_device_drm stay off under xemac; Linux is unchanged (all true).

An imported BO's size came from lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_END) on the dma-buf. An object fd here is an open of a character
device, whose SEEK_END is 0 (checked on macOS), so under xemac the kernel answers it: xemac_obj_size()
(DRM_IOCTL_B580_OBJ_INFO through the device's IOUserClient, never an ioctl on the object fd).

Validation on the build Mac (x86_64 deqp-vk under Rosetta, XEMAC_FAKE=1, the fake device's object fds):
dEQP-VK.api.external.* 550 cases: prod9 61 Pass / 489 NotSupported -> 144 Pass / 406 NotSupported, 0 Fail
(+83: semaphore opaque_fd 20, sync_fd 8, fence opaque_fd 22, sync_fd 9, memory opaque_fd 24; the remaining fd
NotSupported are the dup/dup2/dup3/send_over_socket cases CTS compiles only for Linux/Android). With
XEMAC_FAKE_FDS=0 (a kernel without object fds) all 550 results are identical to prod9.

